{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-energy-equivalence-interpretation","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:mass-energy-equivalence-interpretation","kind":"remark","title":"Regime behaviour, the electron, and pair creation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-energy","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/cor-mass-identity-C","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-energy-electron-check","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-energy-pair-creation"],"foreshadows":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-energy-electron-check","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-mass-energy-pair-creation"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-mass-energy","cites":["references/yekutieli2015"],"text":"mass-energy-equivalence-interpretation.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:mass-energy-equivalence-interpretation\"></a><p><strong>Content of the definition.</strong>\nThe energy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E} = \\mathfrak{m} \\cdot c_q^2</code> (<a href=\"#def:mass-energy\" data-at=\"information-theory/speed-of-light\">energy</a>) rescales the mass by the <strong>square of the information speed</strong>. The factor <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_q^2 = 1/(q-1)^2</code> is the square of the ratio of spatial coupling to temporal coupling in the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-connection. The energy is not the crossing energy (<a href=\"#rem:mass-energy-not-crossing-energy\" data-at=\"information-theory/speed-of-light\">energy is not crossing energy</a>).</p>\n<p><strong>Regime behaviour of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E} = \\mathfrak{m} \\cdot c_q^2</code>.</strong></p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Regime</th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code></th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c_q^2</code></th>\n<th>Physics</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Deep-quantum</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\to \\infty</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\to 0</code></td>\n<td>Energy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\to 0</code> for any mass</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Golden threshold</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varphi^2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 0.382</code></td>\n<td>Sub-relativistic: mass dominates energy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>The observed universe</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q_0</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 83.2</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E} \\approx 83\\mathfrak{m}</code>: large amplification</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Near-classical</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1.01</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">10{,}000</code></td>\n<td>Extreme amplification: tiny mass <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\to</code> large energy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Classical limit</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q \\to 1^+</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\to \\infty</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E}/\\mathfrak{m} \\to \\infty</code>: classical <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E = mc^2</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">c</code> large</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>At <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = q_0</code>, a braid class with mass <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{m}</code> has energy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E} = \\mathfrak{m}/(q-1)^2 \\approx 83\\mathfrak{m}</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Archimedean realisation.</strong>\nOver <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}</code>, Yekutieli's nonabelian multiplicative integral <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"yekutieli2015\">[yekutieli2015]</span> realises the mass (<a href=\"#cor:mass-identity-C\">mass over <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}</code></a>), and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathfrak{E}</code> is that norm divided by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(q-1)^2</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/mass-energy-equivalence-interpretation.md","heading":"Remark","number":"22.4.6","page":"b/rem-mass-energy-equivalence-interpretation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":51,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":36,"unknown":0,"stale":17},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
